{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-53073","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101263","text":"Lane E — the site and the nav"}]},{"id":"blk-53074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101264","marks":["bold"],"text":"Owns:"},{"id":"spn-101265","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101266","marks":["code"],"text":"computedriven.com/"},{"id":"spn-101267","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101268","marks":["bold"],"text":"Must not touch:"},{"id":"spn-101269","text":" root "},{"id":"spn-101270","marks":["code"],"text":"*.md"},{"id":"spn-101271","text":" (lane F), "},{"id":"spn-101272","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT/"},{"id":"spn-101273","text":" (lane A), "},{"id":"spn-101274","marks":["bold"],"text":"`ampersand-nav/` (lane N)"},{"id":"spn-101275","text":". "},{"id":"spn-101276","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: ✅ READY NOW."},{"id":"spn-101277","text":" Nothing blocks the site work; only the pricing copy waits on Travis."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53076","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101278","text":"## OWNERSHIP CHANGE — 2026-08-16  "},{"id":"spn-101279","marks":["bold"],"text":"`ampersand-nav/` is no longer lane E's. It belongs exclusively to lane N"},{"id":"spn-101280","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-101281","marks":["code"],"text":"agents/SITES.md"},{"id":"spn-101282","text":").  This brief and "},{"id":"spn-101283","marks":["code"],"text":"SITES.md"},{"id":"spn-101284","text":" asserted conflicting ownership of the same file for one day, which is the exact failure the ownership contract exists to prevent — an agent following this brief was authorised to edit a file another brief said only its own lane could touch. Caught by GPT on review of "},{"id":"spn-101285","marks":["code"],"text":"SITES.md"},{"id":"spn-101286","text":". "},{"id":"spn-101287","marks":["bold"],"text":"The nav is the one genuinely shared object in the portfolio"},{"id":"spn-101288","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-101289","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-nav.sh"},{"id":"spn-101290","text":" fans one source out to 26 targets across ~21 sub-repos, writing into every site repo), so it needs a single owner and that owner has to run last, alone.  "},{"id":"spn-101291","marks":["bold"],"text":"§3 below is retained as the specification of the work, and is now lane N's to execute."},{"id":"spn-101292","text":" If lane E discovers a nav requirement, it "},{"id":"spn-101293","marks":["bold"],"text":"records it in its report and stops."},{"id":"spn-101294","text":" Lane N consumes those requests at the end."}]}],"id":"blk-53075","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-53077","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101295","text":"Read first"}]},{"id":"blk-53078","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101296","marks":["code"],"text":"COMPUTEDRIVEN_POSITIONING_PLAN.md"},{"id":"spn-101297","text":" §9 (content outline) and §11.2 of "},{"id":"spn-101298","marks":["code"],"text":"WORLD_SIZE.md"},{"id":"spn-101299","text":" (the tier table) · "},{"id":"spn-101300","marks":["code"],"text":"computedriven.com/README.md"},{"id":"spn-101301","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-53079","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101302","text":"What the site is"}]},{"id":"blk-53080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101303","text":"Its own git repo, served through "},{"id":"spn-101304","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cloudflare, not GitHub Pages"},{"id":"spn-101305","text":" — a push reaches the live domain in about 15–30 seconds. One static page, self-contained CSS and vanilla JS, "},{"id":"spn-101306","marks":["bold"],"text":"no build step"},{"id":"spn-101307","text":", nav loaded from "},{"id":"spn-101308","marks":["code"],"text":"/amp-nav.js"},{"id":"spn-101309","text":". "},{"id":"spn-101310","marks":["bold"],"text":"Preserve the no-build-step property"},{"id":"spn-101311","text":"; it is itself evidence for the thesis and must not be traded for a framework."}]},{"id":"blk-53081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101312","text":"Currently 14 sections and ~127 KB. The ladder, tracks, the certificate and the participation rungs went in on 2026-08-15."}]},{"id":"blk-53082","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101313","text":"The work"}]},{"id":"blk-53083","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101314","text":"1. T&R Cloud — the section that was deliberately left off"}]},{"id":"blk-53084","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101315","text":"It was held back because the tiers were gated on a measurement. "},{"id":"spn-101316","marks":["bold"],"text":"That measurement is done and the tiers are un-retracted"},{"id":"spn-101317","text":", so the section can be written."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-53086","spans":[{"id":"spn-101318","text":"Tier"}]},{"id":"blk-53087","spans":[{"id":"spn-101319","text":"Price"}]},{"id":"blk-53088","spans":[{"id":"spn-101320","text":"COGS on R2"}]},{"id":"blk-53089","spans":[{"id":"spn-101321","text":"Margin"}]}],"id":"blk-53085","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-53090","spans":[{"id":"spn-101322","text":"10 GB free"}]},{"id":"blk-53091","spans":[{"id":"spn-101323","text":"$0"}]},{"id":"blk-53092","spans":[{"id":"spn-101324","marks":["bold"],"text":"$0.00"}]},{"id":"blk-53093","spans":[{"id":"spn-101325","text":"genuinely free"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53094","spans":[{"id":"spn-101326","text":"Driver 100 GB"}]},{"id":"blk-53095","spans":[{"id":"spn-101327","text":"$6"}]},{"id":"blk-53096","spans":[{"id":"spn-101328","text":"$1.35"}]},{"id":"blk-53097","spans":[{"id":"spn-101329","marks":["bold"],"text":"78%"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53098","spans":[{"id":"spn-101330","text":"Fleet 500 GB"}]},{"id":"blk-53099","spans":[{"id":"spn-101331","text":"$19"}]},{"id":"blk-53100","spans":[{"id":"spn-101332","text":"$7.35"}]},{"id":"blk-53101","spans":[{"id":"spn-101333","marks":["bold"],"text":"61%"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53102","spans":[{"id":"spn-101334","text":"Factory 2 TB"}]},{"id":"blk-53103","spans":[{"id":"spn-101335","text":"$69"}]},{"id":"blk-53104","spans":[{"id":"spn-101336","text":"$30.57"}]},{"id":"blk-53105","spans":[{"id":"spn-101337","marks":["bold"],"text":"56%"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53106","spans":[{"id":"spn-101338","marks":["bold"],"text":"Enterprise 10 TB"}]},{"id":"blk-53107","spans":[{"id":"spn-101339","marks":["bold"],"text":"[TRAVIS]"}]},{"id":"blk-53108","spans":[{"id":"spn-101340","text":"$153.45"}]},{"id":"blk-53109","spans":[{"id":"spn-101341","marks":["bold"],"text":"~$438 holds 65%"}]}]]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101342","marks":["bold"],"text":"ARITHMETIC CORRECTED 2026-08-16."},{"id":"spn-101343","text":" This row read "},{"id":"spn-101344","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"~$236 holds 65%\""},{"id":"spn-101345","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-101346","marks":["bold"],"text":"$236 holds 35%."},{"id":"spn-101347","text":" $153.45 ÷ $236 = 65.02% — the figure was "},{"id":"spn-101348","marks":["bold"],"text":"COGS as a share of price"},{"id":"spn-101349","text":", which is the inverse of gross margin. A true 65% needs $153.45 ÷ 0.35 = "},{"id":"spn-101350","marks":["bold"],"text":"$438.43."},{"id":"spn-101351","text":" The other three tiers were re-checked and are correct (77.5 / 61.3 / 55.7, printed as 78 / 61 / 56). Caught by GPT reviewing this brief. "},{"id":"spn-101352","marks":["bold"],"text":"The same wrong figure was in five other places"},{"id":"spn-101353","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-101354","marks":["code"],"text":"COMPUTEDRIVEN_POSITIONING_PLAN.md"},{"id":"spn-101355","text":" ×2, "},{"id":"spn-101356","marks":["code"],"text":"WORLD_SIZE.md"},{"id":"spn-101357","text":" ×2, "},{"id":"spn-101358","marks":["code"],"text":"agents/README.md"},{"id":"spn-101359","text":" — all corrected in place the same day.  "},{"id":"spn-101360","marks":["bold"],"text":"This is why the [TRAVIS] gate is drawn where it is."},{"id":"spn-101361","text":" The row was labelled a decision, so the wrong number never reached a page. But it sat in \"settled arithmetic\" for a day, and an agent told "},{"id":"spn-101362","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"the arithmetic above is arithmetic, not a decision\""},{"id":"spn-101363","text":" would have reasoned from it. "},{"id":"spn-101364","marks":["bold"],"text":"Re-derive any margin you are about to publish; do not copy one."}]}],"id":"blk-53110","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-53112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101365","marks":["bold"],"text":"The framing that is true and worth using:"},{"id":"spn-101366","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101367","marks":["italic"],"text":"your world is a graph — back up the graph, restore the world."},{"id":"spn-101368","text":" And the measured fact that makes it good copy: "},{"id":"spn-101369","marks":["bold"],"text":"the world layer is ~0.1% of a 100 GB backup"},{"id":"spn-101370","text":", so the roads, tracks, WRL and provenance ride along free inside a tier priced for bulk. "},{"id":"spn-101371","marks":["bold"],"text":"Unlimited restores are affordable because R2 charges nothing for egress"},{"id":"spn-101372","text":" — that claim is true, sounds expensive, and costs nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-53113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101373","marks":["bold"],"text":"Enterprise is not \"more gigabytes.\""},{"id":"spn-101374","text":" It is "},{"id":"spn-101375","marks":["bold"],"text":"dedicated infrastructure"},{"id":"spn-101376","text":" — own VM, own database, optional data residency. That is what it sells."}]},{"id":"blk-53114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101377","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not publish a price Travis has not set."},{"id":"spn-101378","text":" The arithmetic above is arithmetic, not a decision."}]},{"id":"blk-53115","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101379","text":"2. Keep the rungs honest as they move"}]},{"id":"blk-53116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101380","text":"The page prints an evidence rung per ladder step. On 2026-08-15 REPLAY moved "},{"id":"spn-101381","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-101382","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-101383","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-101384","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101385","marks":["bold"],"text":"the same morning the page was written"},{"id":"spn-101386","text":", and the table was corrected before publishing. That will happen again."}]},{"id":"blk-53117","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101387","marks":["bold"],"text":"Currently accurate and worth keeping accurate:"},{"id":"spn-101388","text":" the page says a track "},{"id":"spn-101389","marks":["italic"],"text":"cannot be published or addressed"},{"id":"spn-101390","text":" and lists \"Drive it\" as not existing. "},{"id":"spn-101391","marks":["bold"],"text":"That is still true from a user's point of view"},{"id":"spn-101392","text":" — seal/store/verify exist "},{"id":"spn-101393","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-101394","text":", nothing is wired into the shell, and nothing has been uploaded to a real host. "},{"id":"spn-101395","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not upgrade that claim until lane A wires it and a real host serves one."}]},{"id":"blk-53118","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101396","text":"3. The nav tier band — plan §6, and the highest-leverage change left"}]},{"id":"blk-53119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101397","text":"One file, "},{"id":"spn-101398","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-nav/src/amp-nav.js"},{"id":"spn-101399","text":", synced by "},{"id":"spn-101400","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-nav.sh"},{"id":"spn-101401","text":" to ~18 sites. Add to each "},{"id":"spn-101402","marks":["code"],"text":"LINKS"},{"id":"spn-101403","text":" entry: "},{"id":"spn-101404","marks":["code"],"text":"tier"},{"id":"spn-101405","text":" (1 Place / 2 Product / 3 Spec / 4 Outside), "},{"id":"spn-101406","marks":["code"],"text":"layer"},{"id":"spn-101407","text":", "},{"id":"spn-101408","marks":["code"],"text":"rung"},{"id":"spn-101409","text":", "},{"id":"spn-101410","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-101411","text":". Render a placement band: tier 1 no band, tier 2 "},{"id":"spn-101412","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"the {layer} layer of ComputeDriven\""},{"id":"spn-101413","text":", tier 3 "},{"id":"spn-101414","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"a specification in the ComputeDriven world\""},{"id":"spn-101415","text":" + link to the real spec, tier 4 nav removed."}]},{"id":"blk-53120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101416","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edit `ampersand-nav/src/`, never a vendored copy."},{"id":"spn-101417","text":" The script fans one source out to 26 targets across ~21 sub-repos."}]},{"id":"blk-53121","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101418","marks":["bold"],"text":"The rung chip must render the stored rung, never a default."},{"id":"spn-101419","text":" Missing renders "},{"id":"spn-101420","marks":["code"],"text":"?"},{"id":"spn-101421","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-101422","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-101423","text":" and not blank — an invented status is worse than a missing one because it stops the question being asked."}]},{"id":"blk-53122","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101424","marks":["bold"],"text":"Check for a dirty tree first."},{"id":"spn-101425","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101426","marks":["code"],"text":"amp-nav.js"},{"id":"spn-101427","text":" has been mid-flight from a parallel session before."}]},{"id":"blk-53123","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101428","text":"Done means"}]},{"id":"blk-53124","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53126","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101429","text":"Live route verified by "},{"id":"spn-101430","marks":["bold"],"text":"serving the domain and checking it"},{"id":"spn-101431","text":", not by grepping the local tree —"}]}],"id":"blk-53125","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53127","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101432","text":"that error mode is recorded in "},{"id":"spn-101433","marks":["code"],"text":"workbench/docs/ROADMAP.md"},{"id":"spn-101434","text":" and it has cost a wrong claim here."}]},{"id":"blk-53128","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53130","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101435","text":"No horizontal overflow at 390 / 700 / 790 / 800 / 815 / 1000 / 1280 / 1600 px."}]}],"id":"blk-53129","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53132","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101436","text":"Every anchor in the nav resolves to a section that exists."}]}],"id":"blk-53131","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53133","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101437","text":"Traps this site has already paid for"}]},{"id":"blk-53134","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101438","marks":["bold"],"text":"`IntersectionObserver` never fires in the Claude browser pane"},{"id":"spn-101439","text":" — it does not composite frames."}]}],"id":"blk-53135","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53137","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101440","text":"A scroll-triggered animation with IO as its only trigger renders as empty troughs. Always add a "},{"id":"spn-101441","marks":["code"],"text":"setTimeout"},{"id":"spn-101442","text":" fallback and a "},{"id":"spn-101443","marks":["code"],"text":"done"},{"id":"spn-101444","text":" guard."}]},{"id":"blk-53138","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101445","marks":["bold"],"text":"The mono font ligatures `|>` into a single `▷`"},{"id":"spn-101446","text":" — pretty, and unsearchable. "},{"id":"spn-101447","marks":["code"],"text":"#cert .wrlbox"}]}],"id":"blk-53139","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53141","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101448","text":"disables ligatures for that reason; the WRL listings keep theirs because "},{"id":"spn-101449","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-101450","text":" reads better as an arrow."}]},{"id":"blk-53142","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101451","marks":["bold"],"text":"The nav hid its links at 780 px but overflowed at 790"},{"id":"spn-101452","text":", so 781–800 scrolled the whole document"}]}],"id":"blk-53143","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53145","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101453","text":"sideways. The breakpoint is 810 now. Measured across eight widths."}]},{"id":"blk-53146","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53148","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101454","marks":["bold"],"text":"`agent-browser screenshot <name>` parses a bare filename as a selector."},{"id":"spn-101455","text":" An element shot of a"}]}],"id":"blk-53147","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101456","text":"tall section came back a uniform black rectangle with the DOM plainly visible. Take viewport shots; resize with "},{"id":"spn-101457","marks":["code"],"text":"agent-browser set viewport W H"},{"id":"spn-101458","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-53150","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101459","marks":["bold"],"text":"Never put an email address on this page."},{"id":"spn-101460","text":" Contact goes through Formspree"}]}],"id":"blk-53151","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101461","text":"("},{"id":"spn-101462","marks":["code"],"text":"https://formspree.io/f/xaewoadr"},{"id":"spn-101463","text":") — Travis's call, 2026-08-11. No "},{"id":"spn-101464","marks":["code"],"text":"mailto:"},{"id":"spn-101465","text":" anywhere, not even as a fallback."}]},{"id":"blk-53154","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53156","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101466","marks":["bold"],"text":"`.jn-count` is hand-maintained."},{"id":"spn-101467","text":" Nothing fetches at runtime. The counts move only in a commit"}]}],"id":"blk-53155","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-53157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101468","text":"that also moves the date."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierazhwlrai7u7rks5bbnfiekr7n6ra73rjaq6smlygranwgtpncawrq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}